  "reply_markdown": "1. **Q1 — choose option 2 with explicit endpoint configuration**, initially for qualified z.ai/MiMo profiles. Ranking (deciding factor → failure mode): **2 explicit**: self-contained configuration → profile drift; **2 referencing Codex**: centralized credential reference → hidden config coupling; **3**: independently versioned policy → duplicated engine contracts; **1**: no demonstrated benefit → forfeited savings; **4**: chores-only scope → no audited reviews. Use a versioned lineage tuple of engine, auth/header mode, canonical HTTPS URL including port/path, and nonsecret credential scope; keep model/window separate. Add an explicit account/plan quota-group ID shared across routes. Preserve existing fingerprints. Subscription billing alone does not force migration: existing Codex plan routes remain available.\n\n2. **Q2 — prefer direct IDs**, but qualify both forms before deciding. Exact init values for these variants were not supplied or observed here. Record selector, frozen alias mapping, init ID and primary assistant/usage IDs; validate a provider-specific mapping, not Anthropic-family matching. Permit syntactically valid IDs; capabilities remain profile/model/version-specific. Preserve context separately from tested `[1m]` normalization. F03-6 remains open: my in-memory test accepted a different final assistant model because the pinned model generated more aggregate output.\n\n3. **Q3 — local preflight by default:** validate route, credential presence and CLI compatibility; no automatic paid probe. Provide an explicit CLI smoke check. Share confirmed account-wide quota failures across the declared plan group; keep endpoint/protocol failures route-local and credential failures credential-local. A generic 429 does not prove plan exhaustion.\n\n4. **Q4 — use explicit authentication profiles.** For bearer profiles inject only `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` and `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`; exclude `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, inherited model mappings and OAuth variables. An x-api-key profile must instead inject its selected key. Kimi's current recipe uses that form; token-only compatibility is unproven. Bound optional `API_TIMEOUT_MS`; use mappings only when qualified. Init alone cannot prove destination/billing: verify egress and provider usage, including invalid-token failure without subscription fallback. [Gateway authentication](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/llm-gateway-connect)\n\n5. **Q5 — classify serving vendor by endpoint for endpoint mode**, before the engine fallback; retain closed model lists and map unknowns to `other`. Handle tested suffixes consistently. Keep model lab independent: GLM via Alibaba remains Zhipu for panel diversity. Export neither endpoint, credential reference nor quota-group ID. Existing code still classifies every Claude-engine record as Anthropic.\n\n6. **Q6 — update the premise:** current [z.ai documentation](https://docs.z.ai/devpack/overview) uses token-weighted credits, not one prompt per call. Confirm any grandfathered account. Measure actual credits per successful review for both providers, including repairs, retries, cache creation and output; calls/cache ratios are diagnostics. Proposed adoption gate: ≥20% cost reduction, paired 95% interval excluding no improvement, ≥95% initial schema success, no material adjudicated quality loss, and p95 latency ≤1.2× baseline. Randomize AB/BA on frozen repositories, control cache state/time pricing, and blind quality scoring. Start with 10 paired briefs/provider; target ≥30 distinct pairs, repeat a subset, and expand from pilot variance. Thirty is not a statistical guarantee.\n\n7. **Q7 — enforce both constraints:** a shared-profile concurrency cap and a shared-plan cap across Codex/Claude, plus session writer exclusion. Endpoint grouping alone cannot replace profile protection. Start profile concurrency at one; raise after qualification.\n\n8. **Q8 — qualify providers individually.** Correct Kimi to its regional [Coding endpoint](https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/), not Moonshot pay-as-you-go. [Alibaba documents interactive-only plans](https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/base-url); read-only tools do not establish headless eligibility. Pin/test CLI upgrades, schema retries, effort and context behavior. Gateway routing does not suppress all Anthropic background traffic.\n\n## Requested checks\n\n- **RC1:** CWD disposable repository/profile; **workspace-write**; compare direct/mapped IDs, new/resume and invalid credentials for each initial provider; capture redacted egress, streams and usage. Settle Q2/Q4; budget six turns/provider, 20 minutes/provider.\n- **RC2:** CWD repository root; **read-only**; inspect current account billing and applicable plan terms for headless reviews. Settle findings #1/#6; budget 15 minutes/provider.\n- **RC3:** CWD isolated frozen checkouts; **workspace-write**; execute Q6's randomized paired pilot and blinded adjudication. Report cost/quality intervals before expansion; budget ten pairs/provider.",
